Modification time stamp: 21.10.20-11:24:13
History id: 1.010
Comment:
The code for throwins has been adapted. It is now possible to specify that
an opponent is thrown in if he wins a trick, but this option contains a
serious flaw. The program cannot handle the situation that an opponent
is thrown in at the moment that he has no cards left.
We added the possibility that a player is thrown in at trick 1. To do
this we specify -Lw[<card>] or -Le<[card>] on the command line to force
a lead at trick 1 rom west or east.

